# Server

The whole backend: a store, four routes, and `Serve on port 8080.`

There is no request-dispatch code here. A `## Route` block says which method and
path it answers, what it takes, and what it returns — and that is the router.
The JSON on the wire is DERIVED from `## A Todo has:` in `shared.lg`, so nothing
in this file serialises anything by hand.

Import Shared.

## Note
Where the list lives. A newline-delimited JSON file, so the demo needs no database
and the file is readable in a text editor while you poke at the app.

## To storePath () -> Text:
    Return "todos.json".

## Note
Read the store, or an empty list the first time the app runs.

A file that does not exist yet is not an error — it is a new install — so this
answers an empty list rather than failing, and the app works on a machine where
nobody has added a todo yet.

The file format is `id|text|done`, one todo per line. It is the server's PRIVATE
storage, not the wire: what a client receives is JSON, derived from `## A Todo has:`
and produced by the route return type. Keeping them separate means the on-disk
shape can change without touching a single client.

## To loadTodos () -> Seq of Todo:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Todo.
    Let mutable raw be "".
    Inspect read(storePath()):
        When Ok (t):
            Set raw to t.
        When Err (e):
            Set raw to "".
    Repeat for line in lines(raw):
        If length of text_bytes(line) is greater than 0:
            Let parts be split(line, "|").
            If length of parts is at least 3:
                Let idText be item 1 of parts.
                Let text be item 2 of parts.
                Let doneText be item 3 of parts.
                If isIntText(idText):
                    Push (a new Todo with id parseInt(idText) and text text and done (doneText is equal to "1")) to out.
    Return out.

## Note
Write the list back in the same private line format `loadTodos` reads.

## To saveTodos (todos: Seq of Todo) -> Bool:
    Let mutable out be "".
    Repeat for t in todos:
        Let flag be doneFlag(t's done).
        Set out to out + "{t's id}|{t's text}|{flag}\n".
    Inspect write(storePath(), out):
        When Ok (v):
            Return true.
        When Err (e):
            Return false.

## Note
`1` when done, `0` when not — the store's own spelling of a Bool.

## To doneFlag (done: Bool) -> Text:
    If done:
        Return "1".
    Return "0".

## Note
The next free id: one past the highest in use.

Counting the list would reuse an id after a deletion, and a reused id makes two
different todos indistinguishable to anything that remembers one.

## To nextId (todos: Seq of Todo) -> Int:
    Let mutable top be 0.
    Repeat for t in todos:
        If t's id is greater than top:
            Set top to t's id.
    Return top + 1.

## Route GET /api/todos -> Seq of Todo:
    Return loadTodos().

## Route POST /api/todos (text: Text) -> Seq of Todo:
    Let todos be loadTodos().
    If text is equal to "":
        Return todos.
    Let mutable next be a new Seq of Todo.
    Repeat for t in todos:
        Push t to next.
    Push (a new Todo with id nextId(todos) and text text and done false) to next.
    Let saved be saveTodos(next).
    Return next.

## Route POST /api/todos/toggle/:id (id: Int) -> Seq of Todo:
    Let todos be loadTodos().
    Let mutable next be a new Seq of Todo.
    Repeat for t in todos:
        If t's id is equal to id:
            Push (a new Todo with id t's id and text t's text and done (not t's done)) to next.
        If t's id is not id:
            Push t to next.
    Let saved be saveTodos(next).
    Return next.

## Route POST /api/todos/delete/:id (id: Int) -> Seq of Todo:
    Let todos be loadTodos().
    Let mutable next be a new Seq of Todo.
    Repeat for t in todos:
        If t's id is not id:
            Push t to next.
    Let saved be saveTodos(next).
    Return next.

## Main

Serve on port 8080.
